WEBVTT

00:01.203 --> 00:05.030
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.031 --> 00:08.168
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.169 --> 00:11.938
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.939 --> 00:14.941
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.942 --> 00:18.219
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.220 --> 00:21.624
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:21.625 --> 00:23.287
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.288 --> 00:25.018
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.019 --> 00:30.201
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:34.990 --> 00:37.676
I tell you, Sundays are
the best, aren't they?

00:37.677 --> 00:39.515
You said it, chief.

00:39.516 --> 00:40.917
Hey, Chris, what's the name of the girl

00:40.918 --> 00:43.387
on the end of the couch?
I'm sure I've met her before.

00:43.388 --> 00:45.689
I'll introduce myself to her.
That'll get her to say it.

00:45.690 --> 00:48.859
Hi. I'm Chris.

00:48.860 --> 00:50.460
Hi, Chris.

00:50.461 --> 00:52.395
Well, that didn't work.

00:52.396 --> 00:54.398
<i>This Sunday
at the Quahog Convention Center,</i>

00:54.399 --> 00:56.466
<i>it's Streaming-Con.</i>

00:56.467 --> 00:58.601
<i>All your favorite YouTubers,
Instagrammers,</i>

00:58.602 --> 01:02.839
<i>social media mavens and digital
influencers under one roof.</i>

01:02.840 --> 01:05.708
Social media? Better swap
my glasses for a monocle

01:05.709 --> 01:08.912
that will pop out when
I'm confronted with modern talk.

01:08.913 --> 01:12.416
<i>LOL at thousands of the hottest
Vimeos, memes,</i>

01:12.417 --> 01:14.717
<i>- epic fails.
- Heavens!</i>

01:14.718 --> 01:18.422
<i>Meet disgraced YouTube star
Logan Paul and his cool bus,</i>

01:18.423 --> 01:19.889
<i>the Golden Throated Homeless Guy</i>

01:19.890 --> 01:21.892
<i>and his cool bus he poops in,</i>

01:21.893 --> 01:23.693
<i>Newly Sober Cat...</i>

01:23.694 --> 01:25.529
<i>formerly Grumpy Cat...</i>

01:25.530 --> 01:27.997
<i>- and teen influencers Tyler Oakley...
- Who?</i>

01:27.998 --> 01:29.565
<i>- Lele Pons...
- What?</i>

01:29.566 --> 01:30.833
<i>- GloZell...
- Where?</i>

01:30.834 --> 01:32.568
<i>- Joey Graceffa!
- When?</i>

01:32.569 --> 01:34.637
<i>- Sunday. I already said that.
- Oh, I'm so embarrassed.</i>

01:34.638 --> 01:36.639
<i>With special guest star,
everyone's favorite</i>

01:36.640 --> 01:40.344
<i>Internet how-to whiz,
Corey from Corey's World.</i>

01:40.345 --> 01:43.046
<i>What's going on, guys?
I'm Corey from Corey's World.</i>

01:43.047 --> 01:44.780
<i>And I'm gonna be live and in-person</i>

01:44.781 --> 01:46.083
<i>at the Quahog Streaming-Con,</i>

01:46.084 --> 01:48.418
<i>where you'll see I'm only five-foot-two.</i>

01:48.419 --> 01:50.654
<i>And remember, that Nazi stuff
I said was in the heat</i>

01:50.655 --> 01:52.522
<i>of a very competitive Halo game.</i>

01:52.523 --> 01:54.790
<i>And congratulations to Goldblatt69,</i>

01:54.791 --> 01:56.860
<i>whose people definitely
do not control the media</i>

01:56.861 --> 01:58.729
<i>and all banking.</i>

01:58.730 --> 02:00.831
Dad, can we go to Streaming-Con?

02:00.832 --> 02:02.565
Well, I wasn't watching
all that closely.

02:02.566 --> 02:03.999
Is it like a rodeo?

02:04.000 --> 02:05.701
Um, sure.

02:05.702 --> 02:07.938
We're going to Streaming-Con! Giddyup!

02:09.840 --> 02:12.676
Looks like someone's
going to Streaming-Con.

02:12.677 --> 02:14.679
Rope a doggy for me.

02:22.619 --> 02:24.887
Oh, awesome. Look over there.
You can take a selfie

02:24.888 --> 02:27.892
in a hospital bed
to get social media attention.

02:30.727 --> 02:33.598
"Don't really want to get
into it, but I'm fine."

02:35.967 --> 02:39.404
Oh, boy. Well, this is
the last thing I wanted.

02:43.607 --> 02:46.877
I'm gonna do a Instagram story
here where I insult a loner

02:46.878 --> 02:49.512
and it becomes a whole thing.

02:49.513 --> 02:53.784
What's up, everybody?
I'm here at Streaming-Con 2019.

02:53.785 --> 02:56.520
Weird ponytail.

02:56.521 --> 02:58.722
They got a whole booth of cat GIFs here.

02:58.723 --> 03:00.456
Jiff?

03:00.457 --> 03:03.460
How-how do you say... Uh-oh.

03:03.461 --> 03:05.662
Hey, man, I didn't say anything
to that guy.

03:05.663 --> 03:07.998
This is ridiculous.
You're hurting my wrist!

03:07.999 --> 03:11.468
So check this out, guys.
I got kicked out of Streaming-Con 2019.

03:11.469 --> 03:13.603
Now, I don't know if anyone
watching this is a lawyer,

03:13.604 --> 03:15.639
especially a constitutional lawyer,

03:15.640 --> 03:16.706
but...

03:16.707 --> 03:18.008
Hey.

03:18.009 --> 03:20.444
Hey, guys, so I'm in my own trunk.

03:20.445 --> 03:21.978
Uh, I think I'm gonna get murdered.

03:21.979 --> 03:23.612
Uh, but before I do, I forgot,

03:23.613 --> 03:25.081
I'm supposed to mention Triscuits.

03:25.082 --> 03:26.682
Really, all the Nabisco products,

03:26.683 --> 03:27.818
they're-they're solid.

03:27.819 --> 03:29.218
You know, like, on the back of Triscuits

03:29.219 --> 03:31.053
when they give you
the recipes for those snacks?

03:31.054 --> 03:32.622
Like, the-the mini pizzas?

03:32.623 --> 03:34.758
I swear to God,
make those little pizzas.

03:34.759 --> 03:37.093
Hashtag it: #PetesTriscuitLifeHacks.

03:37.094 --> 03:38.829
Go ahead and check it out.
Recipe in bio.

03:38.830 --> 03:39.831
Whoa!

03:45.069 --> 03:47.069
I got away.

03:47.070 --> 03:50.773
Hey, guys, I'm in an Uber,
heading back to Streaming-Con.

03:50.774 --> 03:52.778
Uh, man bun alert.

03:57.648 --> 04:00.784
<i>Now seating for
Corey: The Live Experience.</i>

04:00.785 --> 04:02.786
<i>All religions welcome.</i>

04:02.787 --> 04:04.787
That's us! Come on, everyone!

04:04.788 --> 04:05.988
Hey, where's Brian?

04:05.989 --> 04:08.924
Hey, you know how Snapchat
puts a fake dog tongue on you?

04:08.925 --> 04:11.195
How'd you like a real one?

04:12.864 --> 04:15.765
- That was bad.
- Eh, times have changed.

04:15.766 --> 04:17.801
Three years ago, I would've been a hero.

04:17.802 --> 04:19.635
Three years ago, they would've been 12.

04:19.636 --> 04:21.037
I need a nap.

04:21.038 --> 04:23.539
Brian, turn on the heat and NPR.

04:23.540 --> 04:26.642
We now return to NPR's Fresh Air.

04:26.643 --> 04:29.212
<i>My guest today is a white music writer</i>

04:29.213 --> 04:32.214
<i>who has written a book
about the history of hip-hop.</i>

04:32.215 --> 04:34.217
Stewie's loss.

04:34.218 --> 04:36.520
I'm sure this'll be
an enriching discussion.

04:36.521 --> 04:40.222
<i>Hip-hop has its roots in
the call-and-response tradition</i>

04:40.223 --> 04:42.758
<i>of the Southern black Baptist church.</i>

04:56.239 --> 04:58.642
Well, a nap was
just what the doctor ordered.

04:58.643 --> 05:00.440
<i>- I feel like a new...
- And, of course, you can't</i>

05:00.441 --> 05:01.912
write a history of rap

05:01.913 --> 05:04.179
<i>without mentioning Gil Scott-Heron...</i>

05:09.586 --> 05:10.953
What's going on, guys?

05:10.954 --> 05:12.923
<i>I'm Corey from Corey's World.</i>

05:12.924 --> 05:15.125
And today, I'm gonna show you
how anyone can become

05:15.126 --> 05:18.928
<i>an Internet celebrity, like me,
Corey from Corey's World.</i>

05:18.929 --> 05:22.332
I bet you can't make my daughter
Meg an Internet celebrity.

05:22.333 --> 05:23.866
Dad, stop.

05:23.867 --> 05:26.236
No, stand up, young lady.

05:26.237 --> 05:29.104
Rectangle body, fridge bod,
untapped market.

05:29.105 --> 05:30.573
Go with that.

05:30.574 --> 05:32.609
Everybody, hashtag #FridgeBodMeg.

05:32.610 --> 05:34.144
You're welcome.

05:34.145 --> 05:36.145
Oh, my God, Dad!

05:36.146 --> 05:37.880
I'm trending on Twitter.

05:37.881 --> 05:39.149
That's awesome, Meg.

05:39.150 --> 05:42.284
I say we celebrate
by eating Triscuit pizzas.

05:42.285 --> 05:44.654
- Is it good?
- The recipe's right on the box.

05:44.655 --> 05:46.690
- Yeah, but is it good?
- You can make them

05:46.691 --> 05:49.024
with ingredients you probably
already have in the house.

05:49.025 --> 05:51.659
- Dad, what does it taste like?
- That's right.

05:52.597 --> 05:55.632
Ugh! It's like I dropped
a tomato in some hay.

05:55.633 --> 05:58.101
Yeah, it's like if a horse made a pizza.

05:58.102 --> 06:01.239
Triscuits: make sure
you have a drink nearby.

06:06.910 --> 06:08.912
All right, Meg, now that
you're an Internet personality,

06:08.913 --> 06:10.313
we got to build your brand.

06:10.314 --> 06:11.914
Is there anything you can do?

06:11.915 --> 06:13.649
Uh, yeah, actually, I can...

06:17.355 --> 06:19.888
I-Is...

06:19.889 --> 06:22.726
Is there anything you can do
in front of your dad?

06:22.727 --> 06:24.794
- I can shuffle a deck of cards.
- Oh, good.

06:24.795 --> 06:25.928
With my...

06:28.665 --> 06:31.534
All right, we're taking your
bedroom door off the hinges.

06:34.237 --> 06:36.739
Is the lady who owns the Prius here?

06:36.740 --> 06:39.743
- Uh, actually, that's me.
- Oh, well, your wife's car is totaled.

06:39.744 --> 06:41.378
- It's my car.
- Sorry.

06:41.379 --> 06:43.880
We were, however,
able to save your purse.

06:43.881 --> 06:46.061
It's a gender-fluid Euro carrier.

06:46.062 --> 06:48.751
Either way, we'll have it towed
back to San Francisco.

06:48.752 --> 06:51.221
Hey, there are plenty of closer
gay cities, you big ape.

06:51.222 --> 06:52.955
How did this turn into my fight?

06:52.956 --> 06:54.224
You're gonna need a loaner.

06:54.225 --> 06:57.060
We have a pink Volkswagen Beetle
you might feel comfortable in.

06:57.061 --> 06:59.361
Ooh, Brian, we could be two in the pink!

06:59.362 --> 07:00.929
Take that one! Take that one!

07:00.930 --> 07:02.364
Yeah, I'm thinking
of something sportier.

07:02.365 --> 07:05.368
- The red Miata it is.
- Give me your manliest car!

07:05.369 --> 07:06.969
Bill, I need a Hummer.

07:06.970 --> 07:09.238
Again? You're insatiable.

07:09.239 --> 07:10.839
Wise guy.

07:30.828 --> 07:33.697
Wow, that thing's big.

07:33.698 --> 07:35.231
Brian, it's night now.

07:41.439 --> 07:44.407
What's up? This is Refrigerator Meg.

07:44.408 --> 07:47.310
Thought I'd give you a tour
of my refrigerator lifestyle.

07:47.311 --> 07:49.212
Let's see what we've got in here.

07:49.213 --> 07:52.282
Ooh, check, check, check it out!

07:52.283 --> 07:54.017
Boom! Mini cream!

07:54.018 --> 07:56.419
Oh, and what's this? Strawberry yogurt?

07:56.420 --> 07:58.854
Is-is your girl Meg
some kind of health nut?

07:58.855 --> 08:02.694
No, turn it around: 35 grams of sugar!

08:04.494 --> 08:06.361
Yeah, through the roof!

08:06.362 --> 08:08.231
Check it, check it, what's this?

08:08.232 --> 08:10.467
A bacon drawer? Stacked.

08:10.468 --> 08:13.169
Rashers on rashers.
Best part about these bad boys?

08:13.170 --> 08:15.304
Don't even have to cook them.

08:15.305 --> 08:17.708
Cook them right in your stomach!

08:19.243 --> 08:21.446
Wash it down with a little cream!

08:29.186 --> 08:31.790
Oh, boy, that's-that's going
right through me.

08:36.060 --> 08:39.329
Sponsored by Oscar Mayer
and Land O'Lakes.

08:39.330 --> 08:42.065
If it's not Land O'Lakes,
it's not cream!

08:43.933 --> 08:45.969
Hey, Meg? You can't use the Charmin.

08:45.970 --> 08:48.370
You're now sponsored by
Safeway Rough 'n' Thin.

08:48.371 --> 08:50.473
Don't forget to wash the tip
of your middle finger

08:50.474 --> 08:51.810
when you're done.

09:01.451 --> 09:02.719
Mom, we've got a problem.

09:02.720 --> 09:05.488
See, I-I promoted Magic Shell
ice cream topping on my channel,

09:05.489 --> 09:08.123
- so-so they sent me a ton of it.
- Yeah, so?

09:08.124 --> 09:10.128
Dad Han Solo'd himself.

09:11.228 --> 09:13.498
Oh, my God, he's gonna suffocate.

09:19.169 --> 09:22.971
I created a vanilla ice cream
Peter covered in Magic Shell.

09:22.972 --> 09:25.541
- Why?
- Because I must.

09:25.542 --> 09:27.543
Don't listen to him. He's an imposter.

09:27.544 --> 09:29.211
- I'm the real Peter.
- No, you're not.

09:29.212 --> 09:31.113
I made you. I'm the real Peter.

09:31.114 --> 09:33.383
Oh-oh, my God, I-I don't know
which one to believe.

09:33.384 --> 09:36.352
What do you mean?
I'm a guy, and he's ice cream.

09:39.989 --> 09:42.191
Thank God, Lois.

09:42.192 --> 09:45.195
Does anyone mind
if I turn the thermostat down

09:45.196 --> 09:46.797
to 32 degrees?

09:51.235 --> 09:54.604
<i>There ain't a reason on Earth
to waste it</i>

09:54.605 --> 09:58.974
<i>It ain't a crime to be good to yourself</i>

09:58.975 --> 10:00.944
<i> Lick it up</i>

10:00.945 --> 10:02.311
<i>Lick it up...</i>

10:02.312 --> 10:03.580
- Yeah?
- It's me.

10:03.581 --> 10:05.581
Can you change the station?

10:07.384 --> 10:08.852
<i>Whoa, lick it up...</i>

10:09.954 --> 10:11.086
<i>Don't need to wait...</i>

10:11.087 --> 10:13.956
<i>Oh...</i>

10:13.957 --> 10:16.359
<i>Oh, yeah...</i>

10:16.360 --> 10:19.963
Five different stations, all
playing "Lick It Up" by Kiss.

10:19.964 --> 10:21.230
Hummer.

10:21.231 --> 10:23.032
Well, it's nice of you
to once again drive me

10:23.033 --> 10:24.166
to day care, Brian.

10:24.167 --> 10:25.567
Sure. It's only three klicks away.

10:25.568 --> 10:27.936
I just hope I don't
get branded a "Hummer guy."

10:27.937 --> 10:29.339
I can feel the Earth warming.

10:29.340 --> 10:31.139
No one needs a car this big.

10:31.140 --> 10:33.376
Yes, but I like how
when you cut to an outside shot,

10:33.377 --> 10:35.612
Sam Elliott is narrating your drive.

10:35.613 --> 10:38.580
<i>When you need
to take a talking baby to day care,</i>

10:38.581 --> 10:40.048
<i>you'll move mountains.</i>

10:40.049 --> 10:42.618
<i>And if the mountains won't move,</i>

10:42.619 --> 10:45.021
<i>drive right over 'em.</i>

10:45.022 --> 10:47.589
<i>Hummer.</i>

10:47.590 --> 10:51.493
<i>And, yes, Big Lebowski fans,
I've seen the movie.</i>

10:51.494 --> 10:54.331
<i>I don't need to hear the lines.</i>

10:59.503 --> 11:02.372
This place is paying Meg?
Uh, to do what?

11:02.373 --> 11:04.339
Nothing. When you have
a million followers,

11:04.340 --> 11:06.075
people just pay you to hang out.

11:06.076 --> 11:09.211
Yo, yo, yo! Everything here
is made with corn syrup!

11:09.212 --> 11:12.482
Just drink the corn syrup!

11:20.124 --> 11:21.690
Oh, my God, she collapsed!

11:21.691 --> 11:24.426
We got to get her to the hospital.

11:24.427 --> 11:27.229
<i>Don't want to wait
till you know me better...</i>

11:27.230 --> 11:29.932
Anybody need a ride to the hospital?

11:29.933 --> 11:31.066
What?

11:31.067 --> 11:33.536
Does anybody need a ride
to the hospital?

11:33.537 --> 11:35.204
How is she?

11:35.205 --> 11:37.507
- What?
- How is Meg?

11:37.508 --> 11:41.104
I'm worried! Her pulse is very weak!

11:41.946 --> 11:44.648
Her middle finger smells weird.

11:47.084 --> 11:49.238
Meg has Type 2 diabetes.

11:49.239 --> 11:50.651
The one where you're
supposed to shame her,

11:50.652 --> 11:51.838
not feel sorry for her.

11:51.839 --> 11:54.507
But I need to draw
a little more blood for the lab.

11:58.394 --> 12:00.262
As I suspected. Sap.

12:00.263 --> 12:03.065
- Vermont gold.
- I love sugaring season.

12:03.066 --> 12:04.133
Me too.

12:04.134 --> 12:08.037
"The moon, though slight,
was moon enough to show

12:08.038 --> 12:10.506
"On every tree a bucket with a lid,

12:10.507 --> 12:14.142
And on black ground,
a bearskin rug of snow."

12:14.143 --> 12:17.245
Robert Frost,
"Evening In A Sugar Orchard."

12:17.246 --> 12:19.382
Robert Frost!

12:19.383 --> 12:21.283
What? Dad?

12:21.284 --> 12:23.753
It's okay, Meg.
You had a diabetic coma dream.

12:23.754 --> 12:27.124
Dad's still an idiot.
I'm still an idiot.

12:33.730 --> 12:37.466
Coming up, local anchor brings
a concealed weapon to work,

12:37.467 --> 12:39.234
as is his right.

12:39.235 --> 12:42.070
But first, popular
Internet star Meg Griffin

12:42.071 --> 12:43.739
has Type 2 diabetes,

12:43.740 --> 12:47.777
and is also the new face
of diabetes drug Pancresta.

12:47.778 --> 12:49.579
Refrigerator Meg here.

12:49.580 --> 12:53.215
If diabetes has you down,
get your insulin levels up

12:53.216 --> 12:54.584
with Pancresta.

12:54.585 --> 12:56.185
<i>Pancresta may cause heart disease,</i>

12:56.186 --> 12:57.552
<i>swelling, allergic reactions.</i>

12:57.553 --> 12:59.155
<i>Do not take Pancresta
if you are pregnant</i>

12:59.156 --> 13:00.589
<i>or plan on becoming pregnant.</i>

13:00.590 --> 13:02.157
<i>If you have a problem with addiction,</i>

13:02.158 --> 13:04.393
<i>do not take Pancresta,
as smoking Pancresta may mimic</i>

13:04.394 --> 13:06.195
<i>the otherworldly high of heroin.</i>

13:06.196 --> 13:07.796
<i>Chopping up and snorting
Pancresta may amplify</i>

13:07.797 --> 13:10.166
<i>and/or enhance sexual experience.</i>

13:10.167 --> 13:13.069
<i>Rock concerts on Pancresta may
be excessively transformative.</i>

13:13.070 --> 13:15.037
<i>Pancresta may cause
intense philosophical</i>

13:15.038 --> 13:16.471
<i>and scientific breakthroughs.</i>

13:16.472 --> 13:18.541
<i>Pancresta can be delivered
directly to your home,</i>

13:18.542 --> 13:20.743
<i>and since we're here, why not,
we'll do a bump.</i>

13:20.744 --> 13:23.079
<i>Pancresta is not for everyone,
just the sexy people.</i>

13:23.080 --> 13:25.214
<i>Lame losers should not take Pancresta.</i>

13:25.215 --> 13:26.516
Pancresta.

13:26.517 --> 13:29.420
Makes opiates look like
(BLEEP) baby aspirin.

13:32.121 --> 13:34.690
Meg, like everyone
who doesn't have diabetes,

13:34.691 --> 13:36.459
I'm not sure how it works,

13:36.460 --> 13:38.326
but I do know you could go blind,

13:38.327 --> 13:41.196
you could have organ failure,
you could lose your feet.

13:41.197 --> 13:43.498
No amount of fame is worth this.

13:43.499 --> 13:45.634
James Woods High School
will also be saluting

13:45.635 --> 13:47.737
their own diabetic Internet celebrity

13:47.738 --> 13:50.172
with a pep rally in her honor
this Thursday.

13:50.173 --> 13:53.309
Sponsored by Pancresta,
which feels like being inside

13:53.310 --> 13:55.713
the warm, wet mouth of the Lord.

14:04.788 --> 14:07.355
You know, I think you like
driving this Hummer.

14:07.356 --> 14:08.623
You're a Hummer guy.

14:08.624 --> 14:11.761
I'm not a Hummer guy, Stewie.
I'm a responsible Prius driver

14:11.762 --> 14:13.729
who's making the best
of a bad situation.

14:13.730 --> 14:15.531
I didn't ask for this car.

14:15.532 --> 14:17.767
I also didn't ask for these
slowpokes in front of me.

14:17.768 --> 14:20.836
- Out of the way, you old bag!
- Brian, that's Paul McCartney

14:20.837 --> 14:23.638
doing "Carpool Karaoke" songs
we can afford.

14:23.639 --> 14:27.844
<i>She'll be coming 'round
the mountain when she comes</i>

14:27.845 --> 14:29.644
<i>Whoo!</i>

14:32.182 --> 14:33.815
How should we end the scene, Brian?

14:33.816 --> 14:35.685
Sam Elliott or Kiss "Lick it Up"?

14:35.686 --> 14:37.386
Why not both?

14:37.387 --> 14:39.555
<i>"Lick it up. Lick it up.</i>

14:39.556 --> 14:41.423
<i>Oh, yeah."</i>

14:41.424 --> 14:44.227
<i>That's about all I care to read of that.</i>

14:49.666 --> 14:51.801
Refrigerator Meg here

14:51.802 --> 14:53.402
having one of my favorite snacks:

14:53.403 --> 14:55.437
french fry sandwiches on white bread.

14:55.438 --> 14:59.175
Bad sugars and starches are the bomb!

15:04.581 --> 15:07.883
Meg's feet are gone. Rotted.

15:07.884 --> 15:10.719
I have a gift for knowing
when something bad happens

15:10.720 --> 15:14.657
to someone's legs,
kind of like a shining.

15:20.596 --> 15:23.465
<i>How you doing, doc?</i>

15:35.479 --> 15:37.946
Oh, you were thirsty, weren't you?

15:37.947 --> 15:39.614
Good girl. No!

15:39.615 --> 15:41.617
Good boy. You're a boy car.

15:41.618 --> 15:43.618
- Yeah, that's weird. Stop that.
- Stop what?

15:43.619 --> 15:45.187
The way you're touching, feeding,

15:45.188 --> 15:48.257
- and talking to your car.
- His name is Mark McGrath.

15:48.258 --> 15:49.926
What's happened to you?

15:49.927 --> 15:52.894
I-I don't know. All I know
is I love this Hummer.

15:52.895 --> 15:54.530
God, the power.

15:54.531 --> 15:56.431
I deserved a sweet ride
for a little while.

15:56.432 --> 15:58.200
It felt so good.

15:58.201 --> 16:00.503
People turned their heads
when I pulled into Hooters,

16:00.504 --> 16:03.638
Lids, GNC. It's not fair!

16:03.639 --> 16:06.242
- How much creatine...
- I've been doing a lot of creatine!

16:06.243 --> 16:08.243
All set.

16:08.244 --> 16:11.647
You can probably get another
130,000 miles out of this thing.

16:11.648 --> 16:13.916
Well, let's see...
I drive about 4,000 a year,

16:13.917 --> 16:15.785
so when this car goes, I'll be...

16:15.786 --> 16:17.388
Dead for 18 years.

16:18.522 --> 16:20.458
Let me just say goodbye to the Hummer.

16:22.459 --> 16:24.727
I'll miss you, Mark McGrath.

16:24.728 --> 16:26.862
I'll miss scaring the hell
out of homeless people

16:26.863 --> 16:29.632
with your cruise-ship-grade air horn.

16:29.633 --> 16:31.267
I'll miss catching the eye of women

16:31.268 --> 16:33.870
smoking outside of government buildings.

16:41.644 --> 16:44.546
But mostly, I'll miss driving
a military vehicle

16:44.547 --> 16:46.782
45 miles an hour through a school zone

16:46.783 --> 16:49.017
to get Crest Whitestrips.

16:49.018 --> 16:52.321
The back side of this car
is all wrecked.

16:52.322 --> 16:53.855
Who fixed this thing, your wife?

16:53.856 --> 16:56.592
- No, she can't fix a car.
- That's my point.

16:56.593 --> 16:59.961
She passed away last month.
She was addicted to Pancresta,

16:59.962 --> 17:02.530
so she didn't so much
pass away as elevate

17:02.531 --> 17:04.767
to a higher level of consciousness.

17:04.768 --> 17:08.571
Just turned into a smiling beam
of light right before my eyes.

17:08.572 --> 17:11.306
She told me to be at peace, and I was.

17:11.307 --> 17:13.709
I'm hearing a lot of good stuff
about this Pancresta.

17:13.710 --> 17:15.544
Sorry, Mr. Griffin.
I don't know what happened.

17:15.545 --> 17:16.812
Looks like you got the Hummer

17:16.813 --> 17:19.217
for another couple of days at least.

17:20.269 --> 17:22.617
Stewie, why did you do it?

17:22.618 --> 17:24.519
Oh, you were having so much fun, Bri.

17:24.520 --> 17:26.588
Besides, the Earth is on fire.

17:26.589 --> 17:28.707
One dog driving a Prius won't fix that.

17:28.708 --> 17:29.861
Where to?

17:29.862 --> 17:32.627
Let's do donuts on Mark Ruffalo's lawn.

17:32.628 --> 17:34.963
Yeah!

17:36.967 --> 17:39.003
Hey, come on, you guys. Knock it off.

17:40.636 --> 17:42.738
Hey, why don't you turn into the Hulk?

17:42.739 --> 17:44.573
Oh, right. You're just
a Hollywood sissy.

17:44.574 --> 17:45.673
I'm calling the cops!

17:45.674 --> 17:48.376
Oh, you hear that, Brian?
Hulk's calling the cops.

17:54.684 --> 17:56.951
<i>Turns out old Mark really was the Hulk.</i>

17:58.188 --> 18:02.357
<i>And Brian and Stewie got tossed
clear up to New Hampshire.</i>

18:02.358 --> 18:03.625
<i>I'm Sam Elliott.</i>

18:03.626 --> 18:06.529
<i>This concludes your B story.</i>

18:12.368 --> 18:14.036
Look at 'em all out there, Meg.

18:14.037 --> 18:16.037
They're all here because of you.

18:16.038 --> 18:17.972
Hi, Meg.

18:17.973 --> 18:19.909
It's your friends,
Patty, Ruth and Esther.

18:19.910 --> 18:21.943
If anyone remembered what we look like,

18:21.944 --> 18:23.979
it would be shocking how fat we are.

18:23.980 --> 18:26.348
You've inspired us
to gain all this weight,

18:26.349 --> 18:28.383
and we just wanted to say thanks.

18:35.525 --> 18:38.496
♪

18:39.962 --> 18:41.564
Dad, I can't do this.

18:41.565 --> 18:43.699
All my friends are fat because of me.

18:43.700 --> 18:45.735
I don't want them
to lose their feet, too.

18:45.736 --> 18:47.202
Everybody needs their feet.

18:47.203 --> 18:51.440
<i>Feet. Those little
weirdos on the end of your legs.</i>

18:51.441 --> 18:54.979
<i>I used mine to mosey on over
to the A story.</i>

18:56.613 --> 18:58.146
I'm going out there to warn everybody

18:58.147 --> 19:00.149
about the dangers of unhealthy eating.

19:00.150 --> 19:02.485
Meg, I am so high
on Pancresta right now,

19:02.486 --> 19:03.952
I don't care what you say.

19:03.953 --> 19:05.421
Three dimensions?

19:05.422 --> 19:08.090
No, six dimensions.

19:11.127 --> 19:13.094
Be at peace, Meg.

19:13.095 --> 19:14.699
Be at peace.

19:16.566 --> 19:18.568
Phone. Forgot my phone.

19:23.874 --> 19:26.475
- We love you, Meg!
- Eat something gross!

19:26.476 --> 19:28.009
I was gonna take you to prom

19:28.010 --> 19:31.180
as part of a cruel bet,
but I'm fat now, too!

19:31.181 --> 19:33.949
Hey, everybody.

19:33.950 --> 19:36.585
I want to talk to you guys
about something important.

19:36.586 --> 19:38.153
Being healthy.

19:38.154 --> 19:40.588
I'm still Refrigerator Meg!

19:40.589 --> 19:44.125
But from here on, my fridge
will be full of fruits,

19:44.126 --> 19:47.764
vegetables and lean meats! Yo, yo, yo!

19:51.000 --> 19:52.700
Bring back the fridge!

19:52.701 --> 19:54.569
Bring back the fridge!

19:54.570 --> 19:57.739
Bring back the fridge!
Bring back the fridge!

19:57.740 --> 19:58.843
Aah!

20:00.743 --> 20:02.611
What's going on, guys?

20:02.612 --> 20:04.145
<i>I'm Corey from Corey's World.</i>

20:04.146 --> 20:05.881
Did you hear that all the Jewish kids

20:05.882 --> 20:07.884
stayed home from school that day?

20:11.521 --> 20:13.756
Is everyone okay, Principal Shepherd?

20:13.757 --> 20:15.958
Mostly. We only had one fatality.

20:15.959 --> 20:18.193
An old janitor was crushed
under the bleachers.

20:18.194 --> 20:20.996
Huh. Has anyone claimed his feet?

20:20.997 --> 20:23.801
Yeah, and has anyone claimed his mop?

20:28.171 --> 20:32.240
Good news! The feet transplant
was a success.

20:32.241 --> 20:34.108
So...

20:34.109 --> 20:36.880
good news all around.

20:39.682 --> 20:42.183
<i>Well,
I'm glad everything's back to normal.</i>

20:42.184 --> 20:43.652
<i>No, it isn't!</i>

20:43.653 --> 20:45.554
<i>Meg got the dead janitor's feet,</i>

20:45.555 --> 20:48.123
<i>Brian and Stewie got thrown
into New Hampshire by the Hulk,</i>

20:48.124 --> 20:49.792
<i>and you're a beam of light.</i>

20:49.793 --> 20:51.861
<i>I have the shining now.</i>

20:51.862 --> 20:53.761
<i>And Chris has the shining now.</i>

20:53.762 --> 20:55.663
<i>Lois, just do a line of Panc.</i>

20:55.664 --> 20:58.667
<i>Ah! Road House!</i>

20:58.668 --> 20:59.802
Road House.

20:59.803 --> 21:01.703
Road House...

21:01.704 --> 21:03.941
<i>is a movie I was in.</i>

21:03.942 --> 21:07.942
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv